S619 CAULDRON COMPLEXITY AND VARIANT ATLAS
==========================================
DIFFICULTY VERDICT
------------------
Base fixed-k last-boil is Schur-frontier hard, not A000568/LRC/unit-distance hard.
  Reason: the state is a canonical tuple of live sum-free color classes; no S_n graph
  isomorphism, no continuous p0 coimage, and no geometric embedding side-channel is present.
  But k as a growing parameter inherits Schur/Rado-style frontier explosion.
Adversarial, hidden-quotient, LRC, and geometric cauldron variants can be as hard
  as the repo's larger problems because they add alternating quantifiers, orbit
  side-data, all-orders coverage, or embedding obstructions.

